.nh
.TH "TUSK" "1" "May 2026" "Tusk v1.0.0-dev" "Tusk Manual"

.SH NAME
tusk-edge-add - Add a typed edge from one node to another


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtusk edge add [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a typed edge from one node to another.

.PP
The edge kind must be declared in tusk.toml. CLI-added edges are
attributed to a synthetic "\fBcli\fP" source path so the next reindex of
either involved file does not clobber them.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for add

.PP
\fB--source\fP=""
	source node id (workspace-relative path without extension)

.PP
\fB--target\fP=""
	target node id

.PP
\fB--type\fP=""
	edge type (must be declared in tusk.toml)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB-v\fP, \fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	emit debug-level logs to stderr


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  # Mark T-001 as blocking T-002
  tusk edge add --type blocks --source tickets/T-001 --target tickets/T-002

  # Add multiple edges as part of a script
  tusk edge add --type mentions --source tickets/T-003 --target notes/2026-05-16
  tusk edge add --type owned-by --source tickets/T-003 --target people/alice
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBtusk-edge(1)\fP
